    "question": {
      ":question/id": "68eea4e6-d44d-572a-a275-6a78ee9dfd4f",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $A$ given below.\nWhich entries of $A$ could be replaced by $0$ in order to get a matrix in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that by replacing $a_{24}$, $a_{32}$, and $a_{41}$ with $0$, we get a matrix in row echelon form:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\longrightarrow\\,\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe nonzero rows have leading entries in columns 1, 2, 3, in strictly increasing order, and all zero rows are at the bottom. The other options will not give us a matrix in row echelon form.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "7300f7cd-331f-5289-ac55-0e066285e83e",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "5fd8aff0-482e-5a14-ae57-245aec0615d7",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "$a_{11}$, $a_{31}$, and $a_{42}$ only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "5b6b426d-2edd-559b-a0ee-ee9b479904a0",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "$a_{14}$, $a_{33}$, and $a_{44}$ only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "5069f110-c984-538f-a124-b30aefcf089a",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "$a_{12}$, $a_{34}$, and $a_{41}$ only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "75d84267-fdc1-5904-96d6-8730d2f9c5a4",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "$a_{21}$, $a_{22}$, and $a_{41}$ only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "5d5891d7-2785-551b-be81-9435e10f1910",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "$a_{24}$, $a_{32}$, and $a_{41}$ only"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "5d5891d7-2785-551b-be81-9435e10f1910"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
